Z||000000||Tom88gt||12-02-2000||07:02 PM||||I just replaced my dew strips...Rodney, your dew strip tool kicks ass.  <P>Anyway, now the passenger side window "sings" or squeals when being raised.  No noise when it goes down.  If I pull inward a little when raising the window the sound tends not to happen.  Has power windows, if that matters.  The sound is just like when you wet you finger and run it around the rim of a wine glass and make it sing.<P>I don't think there is anything metal scratching the glass but it is still unsettling.||||reg||9
Z||000001||FieroJoe||12-02-2000||11:15 PM||||We had the same thing happening with our new 99 GMC pickup.  Went back to the dealer and they sprayed this "dry-lube" on it, some sort of non-silicone lubricant that wont deteriorate the strips but lubricate them.  I  havent seen it anywhere other than at the dealers, I guess call and ask if they know what I am talking about.<P>Hope this helps!||||reg||1
